From: Brave
Subject: [PATCH] Replace reqwest/tokio/rand with an embedder HTTP transport

Brave performs relay I/O through the Chromium network stack, so the
client uses a pluggable `http::Transport` instead of reqwest, runs hint
requests sequentially instead of via tokio::spawn, and shuffles relays
without rand. The client module is gated on `signing` (secp256k1 only).
---
